By re-defining 'pound' to 500 grams. This is no problem since before
1870 there were some 25 different definitions of pounds (ranging from
400 to 600 grams) in as many independent German states, so nobody
insisted on their pound being the one and only. Other non-SI units
regularily used are 'Zentner'=100 pounds, horsepower=.75*.981kW (defined
via the weight of one kg, hence the .981) and a few other (at,atm,Torr)
for pressure and (ar=100m^2,ha=100ar,Morgen=0.5ha(?)) for field sizes.
Strictly speaking of course cm is also non-SI but nobody really cares.

